; worker.scaly - crash-isolated analysis worker.
;
; The diagnostics pipeline (parser -> modeler -> planner) runs the real
; Scaly compiler, which still SIGSEGVs / aborts / hangs on some inputs.
; Running it in-process would take the whole server down on a single bad
; document. So the parent (server.run) does ONLY transport + dispatch, and
; the dangerous pipeline runs in a persistent child process:
;
;     editor <-stdio-> [parent: transport + dispatch]
;                            |  request  (pipe: parent -> worker)
;                            v  response (pipe: worker -> parent)
;                      [worker: diagnostics pipeline]
;
; Per analysis the parent sends two raw frames (uri, then document text)
; to the worker, then waits for the framed publishDiagnostics payload with
; a TIMEOUT (raw framing avoids JSON-escaping arbitrary document text). If
; the worker crashes (EOF on its output pipe) or hangs (poll timeout), the
; parent kills + reaps it, returns an empty-diagnostics clear for the uri,
; and re-spawns a fresh worker on the next request. The parent thus never
; dies from a compiler bug.
;
; The worker is persistent (one child, many requests) rather than one child
; per request: the pipeline is stateless per document, and the page leak that
; would have made a long-lived worker grow without bound is fixed.
;
; The child is THIS PROGRAM STARTED AGAIN in worker mode (`--scalyls-worker` as
; its first argument, the two pipe ends after it; main.scaly asks
; worker.run_if_worker# before it does anything else) -- fork + exec on POSIX,
; CreateProcess on Windows, behind one question of the OS shim
; (scaly_proc_spawn_self, scaly/fiber/eio.c). It was a bare fork until
; 2026-10-01: Windows has none, and a forked child that carries on without
; exec is a copy of a process whose other threads do not exist in it. The
; worker needs nothing of the parent's memory -- its request loop runs on a
; thread of its own, and every global of this package is thread-local.
;
; CONTROL-FLOW NOTE: `if COND STMT` runs STMT when COND is TRUE (no
; else). One statement per line. CR/LF are numeric bytes (rpc handles the
; framing); quotes are 0x22 bytes.

use scaly.os.File
use scaly.memory.runtime
use scaly.memory.root_pages.getenv
use scalyls.rpc
use scalyls.diagnostics
use scalyls.format
use scalyls.symbols
use scalyls.semantic
use scalyls.tasklens
use scalyls.codelens
use scalyls.placehints

; The process primitives, as questions the OS shim answers (scaly/fiber/eio.c
; and eio_windows.c say what each one promises). Declared here rather than in
; the scaly package: only this package asks them.
procedure scaly_proc_spawn_self(mode: pointer[const_char], mutable out_pid: pointer[i64], mutable out_write_fd: pointer[i32], mutable out_read_fd: pointer[i32]) returns i32 extern
procedure scaly_proc_worker_fds(argc: int, argv: pointer[pointer[char]], mode: pointer[const_char], mutable in_fd: pointer[i32], mutable out_fd: pointer[i32]) returns i32 extern
procedure scaly_proc_reap(pid: i64) returns i32 extern
procedure scaly_proc_wait_readable(fd: i32, timeout: i32) returns i32 extern
procedure scaly_proc_stdio_binary() extern
function close(fd: int) returns i32 extern
function setenv(name: pointer[const_char], value: pointer[const_char], overwrite: i32) returns i32 extern

; The worker's stack, independent of the stack the CLIENT started the server
; with (2026-09-25). The pipeline plans the whole package a document belongs
; to, and the planner's nesting guard is sized from the stack it runs on: at
; `ulimit -s 2048` a codeLens request on dazzle/Style.scaly tripped the guard in
; TeXFOTBuilder.scaly, the worker exited 17, and the client got a successful,
; EMPTY answer -- 0 lenses where there are 15, with the reason on a stderr no
; editor shows. The request loop therefore runs on a thread of this size, and
; the guard's budget is 80 % of it (Planner.stack_budget_bytes#, the same
; ratio), handed over through the planner's own override. 64 MiB is the macOS
; maximum and the size the tree's own tools run at (`ulimit -s 65520`); the
; reservation is virtual, a stack costs the pages it touches.
define WORKER_STACK_BYTES size_t 67108864

; The two pipe ends the request loop serves, handed to its thread.
define WorkerFds (in_fd: int  out_fd: int)

; Wait at most this long for the worker to answer one PER-DOCUMENT request
; before declaring it hung and killing it (milliseconds). Which kinds land
; here is decided by worker.budget_for_kind; SCALYLS_BUDGET_MS overrides it.
;
; ★★★8000 -> 30000 on 2026-08-14, and the old comment shows why: it read
; "well under a second even on the largest file in this tree", which was an
; ASSUMPTION about the single-document pipeline and is false on both machines
; this has now been measured on. Measured here, x86_64 Linux, on a build with
; the same whole-program `opt -O2` the shipped server gets:
;
;   file                        documentSymbol   definition COLD   WARM
;   opensp/Parser.scaly 881 KB       7.17 s          8.72 s       0.14 s
;   dazzle/Primitive.scaly 391 KB    2.39 s         19.81 s       0.06 s
;   scalyls/symbols.scaly  401 KB    2.94 s          3.16 s       0.05 s
;
; A cold `definition` costs 2.5x the old budget on an ordinary file, and
; `documentSymbol` on the largest one sat at 90 % of it with no margin at all.
; ★`definition` itself no longer answers to THIS number — the kind table below
; puts every workspace-walking kind on WORKSPACE_TIMEOUT_MS — but its column
; measures the same cold pipeline, and `documentSymbol` is squarely here.
; ★The warm column is the reason this matters far beyond one slow request: the
; SECOND definition costs 0.06 s, so the budget's job is to protect the very
; state that makes everything after it instant. Overrunning kills the worker
; (worker.shutdown#), the symindex dies with it (symindex.scaly), and the next
; request pays the cold price again — while the client sees a successful
; result, because the parent answers with its fallback. A budget that fires on
; legitimate work is therefore not "a slow path", it is a permanent cold cache.
;
; 30 s covers the measured worst case with ~50 % margin and stays well under
; the whole-tree budget, so the ordering of the three is finally the one the
; work justifies: per-document < completion < whole-tree. It stays finite —
; reaping a genuinely hung pipeline is the whole point of the isolation.
define ANALYZE_TIMEOUT_MS i32 30000

; The whole-tree searches ("w" = workspace/symbol, and the cross-package
; definition / signatureHelp scans that share its index) get their own, far
; larger budget: on a COLD worker they parse every .scaly file under the root
; to build the symindex — measured 6.4-7.4s over this tree's 747 files / 11.6
; MB, i.e. INSIDE the 8s per-document budget but with no margin, so ordinary
; machine jitter pushed them over it.
;
; Sharing one budget was a correctness bug, not just a slow path. Exceeding it
; kills the worker (worker.shutdown#), and the symindex lives ONLY in the
; worker (symindex.scaly), so the kill threw away the very index the request
; was building: the next query started cold, timed out again, and the search
; never completed while every OTHER request paid a fresh worker's respawn. The
; empty `[]` fallback made it silent — the editor sees a valid, successful
; empty result, not an error.
;
; Kept finite so a genuinely hung pipeline is still reaped (that is the whole
; point of the isolation); it only has to exceed a legitimate cold scan by
; enough that jitter cannot reach it.
define WORKSPACE_TIMEOUT_MS i32 60000

; Completion ("c") gets a budget of its own for the same reason, one step down:
; a single request can reach BOTH expensive paths — the session's first
; modeler+planner run for a receiver only the planner can type (measured
; 2026-08-12: 6.0-7.1s once per worker process, 0.05s from the second on) and,
; when the receiver's type lives elsewhere, the cross-package member scan this
; index exists for. On opensp/ContentState.scaly that landed at 8.01s against
; the 8000 ms per-document budget, i.e. the worker was killed and the editor got
; a successful, empty `[]` — and since the kill takes the symindex with it, every
; later keystroke repeated it. 20s leaves margin over the measured cold path
; while staying far below the whole-tree budget: a completion is typed AT, so a
; hang here is felt directly and must still be reaped quickly.
define COMPLETION_TIMEOUT_MS i32 20000

; Worker process state, owned by the PARENT. worker_pid <= 0 means "no
; live worker"; the fds are the parent's ends of the two pipes.
mutable worker_pid: int linked
mutable worker_in:  int linked
mutable worker_out: int linked

; The request loop's thread (serve_on_worker_stack#).
procedure worker_thread_entry(mutable arg: pointer[void]) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns pointer[void] io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig reads prof_list linked

define worker
{
    ; True when the CLIENT has already sent more input: a poll of stdin with a
    ; ZERO timeout, so it never blocks. server.process_one# asks before running
    ; the diagnostics it owes, which is what turns one analysis per keystroke
    ; into one per typing burst (docstore.mark_dirty# has the measurement).
    ;
    ; It lives HERE because the readiness question is declared in this module
    ; for the worker pipes. The answer is exact rather than approximate because
    ; rpc.read_byte# reads stdin with a raw one-byte `read`, unbuffered: nothing
    ; can be sitting in a userspace buffer where a poll of the fd would not see
    ; it. On Windows a stdin that is no pipe (a console, a file) answers "cannot
    ; tell", read here as "nothing waiting": the owed diagnostics run at once.
    procedure stdin_has_input() @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns bool io linked

    ; The whole life of a worker process, when this process is one: main asks
    ; before it does anything else. False in the server itself.
    procedure run_if_worker(argc: int, argv: pointer[pointer[char]]) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns bool io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig linked

    ; ====================================================================
    ; Child side: read framed {uri,text} requests, emit framed payloads.
    ; ====================================================================
    ; Protocol (over the pipe, NOT JSON): each request is FOUR framed
    ; messages — a kind tag ("d" diagnostics / "s" documentSymbol / "c"
    ; completion / "h" hover / "g" definition / "r" references / "l"
    ; documentHighlight / "n" rename / "p" prepareRename / "f" signatureHelp /
    ; "w" workspace/symbol / "o" foldingRange / "t" semanticTokens), the uri, the raw
    ; document text (the parent's in-memory copy; empty = unknown), then a
    ; packed cursor position ("<line> <char>", or "<line> <char> <newName>"
    ; for rename; empty for d/s) — and the reply is one framed payload. Raw framing avoids round-tripping arbitrary
    ; document text through JSON string-escaping (which would corrupt
    ; newlines/quotes/braces). When the document text frame is empty (the
    ; parent has no buffer for this uri) the worker re-reads the file from
    ; disk, preserving the old stateless behavior as a fallback.
    procedure serve(in_fd: int, out_fd: int) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns int io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig reads prof_list linked

    ; Run the request loop on a thread with WORKER_STACK_BYTES of stack and
    ; the planner's guard budget to match (see WORKER_STACK_BYTES). The child
    ; waits for the loop; its own main thread plans nothing.
    procedure serve_on_worker_stack(in_fd: int, out_fd: int) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns int io linked

    ; Handle one request. Returns true to keep serving, false at EOF (the
    ; parent closed its end). A plain (non-#) helper so its local page —
    ; holding the request frames AND the whole diagnostics-pipeline working
    ; set — is reclaimed on return, every iteration.
    ; One request: read it, answer it, and — when SCALYLS_PROF is set — report
    ; what answering it cost. The counters are dumped HERE rather than in the
    ; per-kind branches so the instrument covers every request kind instead of
    ; the one it was built for; an instrument whose scope is narrower than its
    ; name is the trap it exists to prevent.
    procedure serve_one(in_fd: int, out_fd: int) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns bool io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig reads prof_list linked

    procedure serve_request(in_fd: int, out_fd: int) @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns bool io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig reads idx_epoch linked

    ; ====================================================================
    ; Parent side: spawn / kill / analyze.
    ; ====================================================================

    ; Start a fresh worker and record its pid + pipe fds. On any failure
    ; worker_pid stays 0 (analyze then falls back to a clear payload).
    ;
    ; The shim sees to the three things the fork used to do by hand: SIGPIPE
    ; is ignored (writing to a dead worker must be an error, not the parent's
    ; death), the child keeps none of the parent's pipe ends, and its stdin
    ; and stdout are the null device -- if it held the editor's stdout, the
    ; client would never see end of file when the parent exits, and would hang.
    procedure spawn() @deep true io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    procedure ensure() @deep true io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Kill + reap the current worker and close its pipes. Leaves state in
    ; the "no worker" condition so the next analyze re-spawns.
    procedure shutdown() @deep true io mutable worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Analyze (uri,text) in the worker. Returns the publishDiagnostics
    ; payload, or an empty-diagnostics clear payload if the worker is
    ; unavailable / crashed / hung (and respawns it next time). The text is
    ; the editor's latest buffer (the position frame is unused for diagnostics).
    procedure analyze(uri: String, text: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Build the documentSymbol result for `uri` in the worker. `text` is the
    ; in-memory document copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the JSON
    ; array; an empty array `[]` if the worker is unavailable/crashed/hung.
    procedure symbols(uri: String, text: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Hover for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position. `text` is the
    ; in-memory document copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP
    ; hover object, or "" (empty) if unavailable / no symbol at the cursor.
    procedure hover(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Go-to-definition for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position.
    ; `text` is the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the
    ; LSP Location object, or "" if unavailable / no matching declaration.
    procedure definition(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Find-all-references for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position.
    ; `text` is the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the
    ; LSP Location[] array; `[]` if unavailable / crashed / hung / no identifier.
    procedure references(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; documentHighlight for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position.
    ; `text` is the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the
    ; LSP DocumentHighlight[] array (ranges only); `[]` if unavailable / none.
    procedure highlights(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Completion for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position. `text` is
    ; the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the members of
    ; the `.`-qualified receiver under the cursor when it names a declared
    ; concept, else a CompletionItem[] of every declared name; `[]` if
    ; unavailable.
    procedure completion(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; completionItem/resolve: the doc block of ONE entry. `uri` is the entry's
    ; `data` (the file it was read from), `text` the parent's buffer for that
    ; file when it has one — an entry from a file the editor has not opened
    ; resolves from disk, which is the same rule every other request follows.
    ; `packed` is the entry's label. Returns the MarkupContent object, or ""
    ; when the declaration carries no doc block / the worker is unavailable.
    procedure completion_resolve(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Rename for `uri`. `packed` is "<line> <char> <newName>". `text` is the
    ; in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP
    ; WorkspaceEdit, or "" if unavailable / no identifier at the cursor.
    procedure rename(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; prepareRename for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position. `text`
    ; is the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP Range
    ; of the renameable identifier, or "" if unavailable / not renameable.
    procedure prepare_rename(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; signatureHelp for `uri` at the packed "<line> <char>" position. `text`
    ; is the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP
    ; SignatureHelp, or "" if unavailable / cursor not inside a known call.
    procedure signature_help(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; inlayHint for `uri` over the packed "<sl> <sc> <el> <ec>" range. `text` is
    ; the in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP
    ; InlayHint[] array; `[]` if unavailable / crashed / hung.
    procedure inlay_hints(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; foldingRange for `uri` (uri-only, no position). `text` is the in-memory
    ; copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP FoldingRange[] array;
    ; `[]` if unavailable / crashed / hung.
    procedure folding(uri: String, text: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; formatting: the TextEdit[] that re-indents the open document.
    procedure formatting(uri: String, text: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; codeLens for `uri` (uri-only, no position). `text` is the in-memory copy
    ; (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP CodeLens[] array; `[]` if
    ; unavailable / crashed / hung.
    ;
    ; It plans a whole package root, which is the same work "d" diagnostics
    ; already do per document, so it belongs on the per-document budget and
    ; reaches it through budget_for_kind#'s fallthrough — measured 0.45 s for
    ; the scaly root and 2.45 s for dazzle, the largest in this tree, against
    ; a 30 s budget.
    procedure code_lenses(uri: String, text: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; typeDefinition at the packed "<line> <char>" position.
    procedure type_definition(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; prepareCallHierarchy at the packed "<line> <char>" position.
    procedure prepare_call_hierarchy(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; incomingCalls for "<root>\n<name>".
    procedure incoming_calls(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; outgoingCalls for the item declared at the packed "<line> <char>".
    procedure outgoing_calls(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; selectionRange for the packed cursor positions (one per line).
    procedure selection_ranges(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; codeAction for `uri`. `packed` is the newline-separated list of `use`
    ; paths the parent read out of the request's diagnostics. Returns the LSP
    ; CodeAction[] array.
    procedure code_actions(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; The allocation paragraph for the hover at the packed "<line> <char>"
    ; position: where the construction under the cursor lives, or "".
    procedure placement(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Semantic type at the packed "<line> <char>" position. `text` is the
    ; in-memory copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the framed reply
    ; "1<name>" on a hit, "0" on a miss, or "" if unavailable / crashed / hung
    ; (the server decodes the tag and falls back to the lexical hover).
    procedure semantic_type(uri: String, text: String, packed: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; semanticTokens for `uri` (uri-only, no position). `text` is the in-memory
    ; copy (empty -> worker reads disk). Returns the LSP {"data":[...]} object;
    ; an empty-data object if unavailable / crashed / hung. The fallback is
    ; built with quote BYTES (string-literal escapes are not decoded).
    procedure semantic_tokens(uri: String, text: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; workspace/symbol: search every .scaly file under `root` for declarations
    ; matching `query`. `root` rides in the uri frame, `query` in the position
    ; frame; the text frame is unused. Returns SymbolInformation[]; `[]` if
    ; unavailable / no root / no match.
    procedure workspace_symbols(root: String, query: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked

    ; Send one (kind,uri,text,position) request to the worker and return its
    ; framed reply, or `fallback` if the worker is unavailable / crashed /
    ; hung. Up to two attempts: a worker that crashed mid-request is reaped
    ; and the request retried once on a fresh worker, so a transient crash is
    ; invisible to the editor. A deterministically-crashing input falls
    ; through to the fallback after the retry (bounded — no respawn storm).
    ; The response budget for ONE request kind, in milliseconds.
    ;
    ; The question is not how interactive a request feels but whether its
    ; handler can WALK THE WORKSPACE — because that walk is what builds the
    ; symindex, and exceeding the budget kills the worker (worker.shutdown#),
    ; which throws the index away. A budget too small for an index-building
    ; request is therefore not "a slower answer": it is an answer that can
    ; never arrive, since every retry starts cold and dies at the same point.
    ;
    ; ★Measured 2026-08-12 on packages/opensp/ContentState.scaly, three
    ; consecutive inlayHint requests in ONE session: 8.01 s, 9.01 s, 8.00 s,
    ; each returning an empty array with the worker dying in between. 8.01 s
    ; against an 8000 ms budget is not a coincidence — it IS the budget, and
    ; inlayHint fires on every visible-range change, so this ran on every
    ; scroll and took the index for every OTHER request with it. The two
    ; raised budgets that existed named `w` and `c` only, while the comment on
    ; WORKSPACE_TIMEOUT_MS already claimed definition and signatureHelp were
    ; covered; they were not. Hence a table with every letter in it, so the
    ; next kind added has to answer the question rather than inherit it.
    ;
    ; WORKSPACE — walks the tree / builds the index:
    ;   w workspace/symbol   the whole tree by definition
    ;   g definition         current file, then siblings, then the package tree
    ;   r references         every file under the root
    ;   n rename             the same scan as references
    ;   f signatureHelp      find_signature_in_workspace#
    ;   u typeDefinition     resolves a type name, then searches for it
    ;   k prepareCallHierarchy  may locate a routine declared elsewhere
    ;   i incomingCalls      reads every file under the root, like references
    ;   j outgoingCalls      resolves each callee, which may leave the file
    ;   y inlayHint          resolves each call site through f's machinery
    ;   t semanticTokens     cross-package name harvest (nameset.scaly)
    ; COMPLETION — runs the modeler+planner, whose FIRST run in a worker
    ; process costs seconds and every later one 0.05 s:
    ;   c completion         plus the cross-package member scan
    ;   x semantic type      the planner-resolved type behind hover
    ; ANALYZE — parse or lex of the OPEN DOCUMENT only, no other file read:
    ;   d diagnostics   s documentSymbol   h hover (lexical fallback)
    ;   l documentHighlight   p prepareRename   o foldingRange
    ;   a codeAction (a line scan; the planner already did the thinking)
    ;   e selectionRange (a bracket walk over the open document)
    ;   v completionItem/resolve — it parses the ONE file the entry's `data`
    ;     names and reads the comment block above one declaration. It is here
    ;     rather than with the workspace kinds BY CONSTRUCTION, not by luck:
    ;     the file is carried in the entry, so there is nothing to search for.
    ; `SCALYLS_BUDGET_MS=<n>` overrides EVERY budget below with n milliseconds.
    ; It exists for the same reason `SCALYC_STACK_BUDGET` does in the planner:
    ; the guard it tunes trips on a threshold no test can reach reliably on an
    ; arbitrary machine, so without a knob the give-up path is untestable and
    ; stays untested. Set it small to prove the path fires; set it large when a
    ; genuinely huge workspace needs more than the table allows. 0 or unset =
    ; the table. A value that does not parse as a positive number is IGNORED
    ; rather than treated as 0 — a typo must not disable the hang detector.
    procedure budget_override() @ret_nonlocal true @deep true returns i32 io linked

    procedure budget_for_kind(kind: String) @deep true returns i32 io linked

    procedure exchange(kind: Slice[char], uri: String, text: String, position: String, fallback: String) @page true @direct true @deep true returns String io mutable dir_slots, idx_epoch, idx_slots, lc_active, lc_col, lc_data, lc_len, lc_line, lc_off, modeler_error_count, ph_blob_data, ph_blob_len, ph_hash, ph_path_data, ph_path_len, ph_used, prof_bytes, prof_fresh, prof_list, prof_read, prof_sig, worker_in, worker_out, worker_pid reads worker_pid linked
}
